{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/808404-that-time-someone-said-or-did-something-racist-or-offensive-in-your-scion-game","id":808404,"title":"that time someone said or did something racist or offensive in your Scion game","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-01-13T20:00:58-08:00","id":808404,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon5.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> that time someone said or did something racist or offensive in your Scion game","content":"One cool thing about Scion is its wide-ranging representation of world religion and culture. One problem with Scion is that its wide-ranging representation of world religion and culture sometimes sets players up to say or do racially or religiously insensitive things. Has there ever been a moment in your Scion game where you or another player said or did such a thing? How did it come about, and what happened?<br /> <br /> As we go forward with Second Edition, we'd like to give players tools to prevent those mistakes from happening, or\u2014more importantly\u2014to respond kindly, thoughtfully, and productively when they crop up. To be clear, if you think racism and religious intolerance in your group or in Scion in general aren't a problem, that's great! But this thread is for talking about the exceptions.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><a href=\"https://jamesmendezhodes.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Mendez</span></a></span></div> <span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><b>Currently Developing</b> you know I should probably stop updating this field, I keep accidentally announcing things early<br /> <b>Crowdfund Me </b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mndz\" target=\"_blank\">via Patreon</a>: essays about race, religion, and culture in gaming</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8310-lula","name":"Lula","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8310_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T05:36:28-08:00","id":808596,"title":"","content":"Various examples of &quot;Lets have a Native American Pantheon!&quot; and the resulting mess of cultural and ethnic melting pots that stem from this basic misconception.<br /> <br /> Portraying the Pesedjet and their historical counterpart culture as Sub-Saharan African (Black) because they happen to be on the continent of Africa.<br /> <br /> Various, conscious and unconscious variations of meticulously researching and trying to culturally emulate the Amatsukami down to the fine details of what honorific to call someone, but every other culture gets the &quot;Generic Modern Westerner&quot; treatment because they can't be bothered to learn anything about the culture and people.<br /> <br /> I was once told explicitly and I quote &quot;I don't think a scion of Odin would accept a son with the virtue of Intelligence&quot;, after a bit of digging around that train of logic the reason they thought this was because, you know, barbarians and stuff.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3835-\u00falfh\u00e9\u00f0nar","name":"\u00dalfh\u00e9\u00f0nar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T12:43:47-08:00","id":808964,"title":"","content":"One time, my group was playing a scene where we were helping an NPC daughter of Tezcatlipoca rescue a girl who was turning into a were-jaguar.<br /> <br /> Apparently, my friends decided to completely ignore my carefully prepared primer on &quot;Gods With Whom You Do NOT Want To Fuck,&quot; (in which Tezcatlipoca featured prominently) and decided to be all kinds of rude and disrespectful to him. (Yes, they knew who he was. He made no effort to conceal his identity.) One of them went so far as to tell him that his people just mow his yard now.<br /> <br /> Does that count?<br /> <br /> Yeaaaah. I'm still not sure exactly how to deal with that level of stupidity. By rights, I should've had Tezcatlipoca kill the entire Band right there and force my friends to create all-new (and hopefully non-retarded) characters.<br /> <br /> Necessary Disclaimer: My friend who made that comment is not actually racist. He was in-character and he got caught up in the moment. Still a ridiculously insensitive thing to say though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">&quot;We have done the impossible, and that makes us mighty.&quot;<br /> Captain Malcolm Reynolds</div>","edited":{"userid":679,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","user":"unnatural1","date":". 01-14-2016, 03:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","name":"unnatural1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T13:26:30-08:00","id":809027,"title":"","content":"@unnatural1: You're the ST for the lawnmower story? Neat!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T14:55:58-08:00","id":809121,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/808404-that-time-someone-said-or-did-something-racist-or-offensive-in-your-scion-game?p=809027#post809027\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@unnatural1: You're the ST for the lawnmower story? Neat!</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep. That was MY merry bunch of idiots.<br /> <br /> I still can't process what was going through their heads that night. SMH.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">&quot;We have done the impossible, and that makes us mighty.&quot;<br /> Captain Malcolm Reynolds</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","name":"unnatural1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-15T02:57:26-08:00","id":809461,"title":"","content":"Basically any situation with Set is inherently racist. His description even says that he appears as a weasley foreigner, so hes cut out for that kind of situation. Which, in my book, is fine as long as nobody is serious about this. Thankfully I know my players well enough to be certain that isn't the case.<br /> <br /> Also there has been a situation with Tezcatlipoca in my group as well. Our Sun-Wukong Scion, confronted with the task to go to Mexico, asked him straight in the face: &quot;What does Mexico have?&quot; and then, after a second of thinking: &quot;Ooooh! Tacos!&quot; He lost a few teeth for that one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8325,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8325-asmael","user":"Asmael","date":". 01-15-2016, 06:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8325-asmael","name":"Asmael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8325_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-15T17:56:45-08:00","id":809962,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>unnatural1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/808404-that-time-someone-said-or-did-something-racist-or-offensive-in-your-scion-game?p=808964#post808964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One time, my group was playing a scene where we were helping an NPC daughter of Tezcatlipoca rescue a girl who was turning into a were-jaguar.<br /> <br /> Apparently, my friends decided to completely ignore my carefully prepared primer on &quot;Gods With Whom You Do NOT Want To Fuck,&quot; (in which Tezcatlipoca featured prominently) and decided to be all kinds of rude and disrespectful to him. (Yes, they knew who he was. He made no effort to conceal his identity.) One of them went so far as to tell him that his people just mow his yard now.<br /> <br /> Does that count?<br /> <br /> Yeaaaah. I'm still not sure exactly how to deal with that level of stupidity. By rights, I should've had Tezcatlipoca kill the entire Band right there and force my friends to create all-new (and hopefully non-retarded) characters.<br /> <br /> Necessary Disclaimer: My friend who made that comment is not actually racist. He was in-character and he got caught up in the moment. Still a ridiculously insensitive thing to say though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. Yes, that definitely counts. Normally I caution against punitive STing, but I might look the other way for that one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><a href=\"https://jamesmendezhodes.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Mendez</span></a></span></div> <span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><b>Currently Developing</b> you know I should probably stop updating this field, I keep accidentally announcing things early<br /> <b>Crowdfund Me </b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mndz\" target=\"_blank\">via Patreon</a>: essays about race, religion, and culture in gaming</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8310-lula","name":"Lula","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8310_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-16T17:49:46-08:00","id":810418,"title":"","content":"I think in a game about mythology and dead/mostly dead religions it's kind of tough to avoid stereotypes. How would you put something in the game to handle this? The players not offending the rest of the table is part of the necessary social contract inherent in gaming. A simple &quot;not cool man&quot; generally suffices and if it doesn't, well there's a reason I don't game with the guy who only played stereotypical french lesbians any more.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying the problem doesn't come up, there are more than enough gamers with poor social skills, but I don't think a game can address a topic like that that has been causing strife since the beginning of human existence if the individual groups can't do it on their own. The closest you'd get is possibly a sidebar of &quot;check everyone's comfort levels before starting the campaign&quot;.<br /> <br /> Sorry if that went off topic there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8375-vonpenguin","name":"vonpenguin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-24T19:00:13-08:00","id":815809,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vonpenguin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/808404-that-time-someone-said-or-did-something-racist-or-offensive-in-your-scion-game?p=810418#post810418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think in a game about mythology and dead/mostly dead religions it's kind of tough to avoid stereotypes. How would you put something in the game to handle this? The players not offending the rest of the table is part of the necessary social contract inherent in gaming. A simple &quot;not cool man&quot; generally suffices and if it doesn't, well there's a reason I don't game with the guy who only played stereotypical french lesbians any more.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying the problem doesn't come up, there are more than enough gamers with poor social skills, but I don't think a game can address a topic like that that has been causing strife since the beginning of human existence if the individual groups can't do it on their own. The closest you'd get is possibly a sidebar of &quot;check everyone's comfort levels before starting the campaign&quot;.<br /> <br /> Sorry if that went off topic there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not off topic, that's a great question. It's definitely part of that necessary social contract, but not everyone\u2014new players and groups especially\u2014knows about social contracts inherent in gaming. I was thinking about some text pointing out common problems that come up when you're role-playing in this kind of cultural territory and examples of constructive ways to respond when you or someone else makes a mistake, the kind of discussion we're having here. We learn lots of social skills in the metagame space; sportsmanship is a really good example. When I learned to wrestle as a kid, treating my opponent fairly and grace in victory and defeat weren't inherent to the mechanics of wrestling (although traditions such as the handshake do point towards sportsmanship), but our coaches taught us verbally and through demonstration how to operate in the social space surrounding the game. Text isn't as good as a living, seasoned coach, but it's way better than nothing, and can introduce topics which an inexperienced player might think to ask a friend about or research on their own, sometimes even presenting them in stronger language than we might feel comfortable using when we speak to friends or acquaintances.<br /> <br /> When I or someone I'm talking with says something racist in real life, I have some social mechanics that I rely on to respond. &quot;Not cool man&quot; is concise and effective when it works, but it's sometimes not enough if, for example, I say something racist in good faith but don't realize how or why the thing I said is hurtful. Jay Smooth's video about <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=b0Ti-gkJiXc\" target=\"_blank\">how to tell someone they sound racist</a> was really helpful to me here. More RPG-specific tools are <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/x-card-rpg\" target=\"_blank\">John Stavropoulos's X Card</a>, or the Cut and Brake keywords used in LARP.<br /> <br /> We can't eradicate racism or other injurious behavior at the table, but we can help by suggesting productive ways to talk about the subject.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><a href=\"https://jamesmendezhodes.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Mendez</span></a></span></div> <span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><b>Currently Developing</b> you know I should probably stop updating this field, I keep accidentally announcing things early<br /> <b>Crowdfund Me </b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mndz\" target=\"_blank\">via Patreon</a>: essays about race, religion, and culture in gaming</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8310-lula","name":"Lula","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8310_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-24T19:17:43-08:00","id":815820,"title":"","content":"It's a game about ancient pagan religions who practiced slavery, xenophobia, genocide and human sacrifice. I would be very disappointed if we didn't run into offensive content. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> As long as it's in character, I don't see any reason to censor my players. White Wolf games are typically directed towards a mature audience anyways. Heck, the Scion books have a lot of frontal nudity in them to begin with.<br /> <br /> So yeah, as long as it's kept in character, I think it's perfectly alright. If it elevates into an out of character theological debate, then you've got to <b>shut it down immediately</b> because those things can spiral out of control right quick.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 01-24-2016, 10:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-24T19:24:19-08:00","id":815824,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/808404-that-time-someone-said-or-did-something-racist-or-offensive-in-your-scion-game?p=815820#post815820\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As long as it's in character, I don't see any reason to censor my players. White Wolf games are typically directed towards a mature audience anyways. Heck, the Scion books have a lot of frontal nudity in them to begin with.</div> </div> </div> </div>If your players are down with it, awesome. Me, I run a lot of games at conventions with complete strangers and/or first-time players, so I step a little lighter than many other STs, even when I'm running something that runs full speed ahead at racism like Steal Away Jordan or Dog Eat Dog.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><a href=\"https://jamesmendezhodes.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Mendez</span></a></span></div> <span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><b>Currently Developing</b> you know I should probably stop updating this field, I keep accidentally announcing things early<br /> <b>Crowdfund Me </b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mndz\" target=\"_blank\">via Patreon</a>: essays about race, religion, and culture in gaming</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8310-lula","name":"Lula","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8310_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-24T19:39:27-08:00","id":815830,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lula</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/808404-that-time-someone-said-or-did-something-racist-or-offensive-in-your-scion-game?p=815824#post815824\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If your players are down with it, awesome. Me, I run a lot of games at conventions with complete strangers and/or first-time players, so I step a little lighter than many other STs, even when I'm running something that runs full speed ahead at racism like Steal Away Jordan or Dog Eat Dog.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> If a character is uneasy about a Scion of the Loa being in his band because he thinks they'll steal his shit. That's a tolerable form of racism if it's done right. Heck, it may even play a role in character development if the Loa's presence causes them to overcome such paranoia. If that character flings about racial slurs and is Klansmen, then yeah, I think I would have to address that issue. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-24T23:02:35-08:00","id":815911,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/808404-that-time-someone-said-or-did-something-racist-or-offensive-in-your-scion-game?p=815830#post815830\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's a tolerable form of racism if it's done right.</div> </div> </div> </div>How do you do it right, and how did you learn how to do it right? Serious question, actually quite interested.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><a href=\"https://jamesmendezhodes.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Mendez</span></a></span></div> <span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><b>Currently Developing</b> you know I should probably stop updating this field, I keep accidentally announcing things early<br /> <b>Crowdfund Me </b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mndz\" target=\"_blank\">via Patreon</a>: essays about race, religion, and culture in gaming</span>","edited":{"userid":8310,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8310-lula","user":"Lula","date":".  clarifying positive tone 01-25-2016, 02:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8310-lula","name":"Lula","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8310_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-25T06:38:17-08:00","id":816056,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lula</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/808404-that-time-someone-said-or-did-something-racist-or-offensive-in-your-scion-game?p=815911#post815911\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do you do it right, and how did you learn how to do it right? Serious question, actually quite interested.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> By done right, I mean from a character development standpoint. Maybe when the band starts out, racial prejudice causes tension between the bandmates. But over time, during the course of their adventures, they come to trust and depend on each other, overcoming said prejudice.<br /> <br /> <br /> Alternatively, can also make for some nice villains. Heck, they already wrote a story that takes place during Nazi Germany which I'm pretty sure is nothing but racist overtones. :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 01-25-2016, 10:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}